## Variables in JavaScript

Modern JavaScript uses `const` for variables that should not be reassigned, and `let` for variables that will change.

```javascript
const maxScore = 100;
let currentScore = 0;
currentScore += 10;
```

## Reading Input in Node.js

In Node.js coding environments, input is read from `/dev/stdin` or `process.stdin`.

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const input = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();
const num = parseInt(input, 10);
```

